netpoisson (0.2.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Web dashboard: WorldMan themes (dark-x-files default), Capture/Analyse
    panels, Lang/Theme switcher with localStorage, and i18n packs under
    src/web_i18n/<locale>.json (not gettext/po).
  * Raw events 3D: Front/Top/Free/Spectrum, Fit + Keep-aspect, Swing ±5–20°,
    hover tips, angle HUD; top-down from +Y; Z log via log1p; canvas fills
    Capture viewport with Live stats pinned to the bottom.
  * Live λ/bucket/status via POST /api/config; runnings/raw dense windows;
    auto --window with POST /api/window; session bytes with grouped units.
  * Install: bash launcher (netpoisson.in) in bindir; Python under
    /usr/lib/netpoisson; split web page assets for packaging/lint.
  * Docs: refresh L1 man web sections and README i18n notes.

 -- Lenik (谢继雷) <lenik@bodz.net>  Mon, 21 Sep 2026 21:00:00 +0800

netpoisson (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Redesign wire protocol, client validation, SSH stdio, and timelines.
  * Document binary length-prefixed and SSH @nPoi NDJSON protocols.
  * Absolute Poisson schedule, client validation, four timelines,
    telemetry trailer.
  * SSH stdio transport, systemd --install/--remove, web bandwidth and
    session bytes.
  * Split long modules into traffic/, peer_client/, and npcli/ packages
    (ZL0001).
  * Add --tls for TCP and PSK datagram sealing for UDP; default web port
    3871.

 -- Lenik (谢继雷) <lenik@bodz.net>  Mon, 21 Sep 2026 16:25:06 +0800

netpoisson (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Replace the example utility with a Poisson traffic tester.
  * Echo requests unchanged and answer STATUS with server timelines and
    queues.
  * Show scrolling Req/Resp lines, a JSON report, and a live web
    dashboard.
  * Align packaging with zephyr style: noarch RPM, Architecture all,
    scripts/, i18nutil.
  * Split peer I/O into netio_sock, peer_server, and peer_client
    modules.
  * Add L1 whole-document man translations and install them under
    mandir/<locale>/man1.
  * Install locale man pages into DESTDIR instead of absolute /usr
    paths.

